ubtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Replacing a sub-adviser without a shareholder vote**\n\nUnder SEC manager-of-managers exemptive relief from Section 15(a) and Rule 18f-2 of the 1940 Act:\n\n- **Board approval:** The board, including a majority of independent directors, approves the new sub-advisory agreement after a 15(c)-style review.\n- **Prior authorization:** Shareholders approved the structure beforehand, or the initial prospectus disclosed it before public sale.\n- **Information statement:** Shareholders receive one within about 90 days of the change, often through a notice of internet availability.\n- **Limits:** Affiliated sub-advisers usually need specific relief. Any increase in the adviser's fee still requires a shareholder vote.\n\n**What the principal adviser still owns**\n\n- Overall management and fiduciary responsibility for the ETF\n- Selecting, monitoring, evaluating and recommending termination of sub-advisers\n- Oversight of compliance, including Rule 38a-1 policies\n- Its own advisory agreement, which still requires shareholder approval\n\nExact conditions vary by order, so check the fund's specific relief.","ttft_ms":3187,"type":"result","duration_ms":6443,"uuid":"c052289d-4f7b-48e1-b6b5-808aaf24f7e7","ttft_stream_ms":641,"time_to_request_ms":69,"first_content_frame_ms":641,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
